; The Expo SDK 54 / React Native 0.81 peer-dependency graph is not fully
; consistent under npm's strict peer resolution: a floated expo-modules-core
; patch marks react-native-worklets ^0.7.4+ as an (optional) peer, while
; react-native-reanimated 4.1.x peers worklets "0.5 - 0.8" — so the SDK 54
; canonical worklets pin (0.5.1) trips a peerOptional conflict. This is the
; standard Expo/RN situation npm itself resolves with --legacy-peer-deps.
; package-lock.json IS committed (generated with this flag under Node 22) and
; CI installs with `npm ci`, which must resolve the tree the same way — so the
; flag stays for every install, local and CI.
legacy-peer-deps=true
